0.6124,"playId":"401866455341","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3985","guid":"e814c788-dc4b-3d24-b8e7-bb6dd7a1fb3e","fullName":"Warren McGuirk Alumni Stadium","address":{"city":"Amherst","state":"MA","zipCode":"01003","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/3985.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":8881},"article":{"headline":"Watson's 13-yard TD run in OT lifts UMass over Ball State 31-30","description":"— William Watson III broke loose for a 13-yard touchdown run in overtime to give Massachusetts a 31-30 victory over Ball State on Wednesday night.","story":"AMHERST, Mass. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4920153/william-watson\" target=\"_new\">William Watson III</a> broke loose for a <a href=\"https://x.com/UMassFootball/status/2118183776870392214?a=SAnPPdUAvO7qcI7--UKM&s=20\">13-yard touchdown run in overtime</a> to give Massachusetts a 31-30 victory over Ball State on Wednesday night. \n\n\r\n              Ball State quarterback <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5075392/keldric-luster\" target=\"_new\">Keldric Luster</a> scored on a 2-yard run with 25 seconds left in regulation to end a nine-plane, 75-yard drive that tied it 24-all.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5265528/jalen-bonds\" target=\"_new\">Jalen Bonds</a>, who finished with 132 yards rushing on 17 carries, scored from a yard out for the Cardinals on the first possession of overtime, but Brody Boehm’s extra-point attempt was wide left. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5218751/derek-morris\" target=\"_new\">Derek Morris</a>, who missed a 36-yard field-goal attempt in the first quarter but was good on a 23-yarder in the third, converted the extra point in OT for UMass. \n\n\r\n              Watson completed 17 of 25 passes for 302 yards. He tossed a 64-yard touchdown pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5388332/jabari-lewis\" target=\"_new\">Jabari Lewis</a> just before halftime to give UMass a 14-10 lead, and his 1-yard TD run gave the Minutemen a 21-17 advantage with 2:31 to play in the third quarter. \n\n\r\n              Curtis Kimmons had 85 yards rushing and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5264764/elijah-faulkner\" target=\"_new\">Elijah Faulkner</a> scored from a yard out for UMass (5-4, 2/3 Mid-American Conference), which snapped a four-game losing streak. \n\n\r\n              Luster was 17-of-27 passing for 182 yards and threw a touchdown pass for Ball State (3-6, 2-3). \n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Ball State: Hosts Buffalo next Wednesday. \n\n\r\n              UMass: At Toledo next Wednesday. \n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>, visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-05T04:16:33Z"}}